What is a White Light Endoscope?
A white light endoscope is a diagnostic and therapeutic device that transmits broad‑spectrum visible light through a fiber‑optic or electronic imaging channel to illuminate internal anatomical structures. The technology enables clinicians to obtain high‑contrast, true‑color images of mucosal surfaces, facilitating accurate lesion detection, targeted biopsies, and a variety of minimally invasive interventions. Modern iterations incorporate high‑definition sensors, ergonomic designs, and increasingly sophisticated software layers such as AI‑driven polyp‑detection algorithms.
